{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-34601" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the value of ${x}_{3}-{x}_{4}$ given that  $6a-2x=b$ and\n\n$$\na=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 8\\end{aligned}],\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{4}\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ -6 \\\\ -12 \\\\ -10\\end{aligned}].\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14061066/state.json" "file_sha256" "b4c3b9da0d15be78d0b279405751f68553deb47cd07086a9c5fb811a41ef3ce8"} {"question" "q-34601" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Using the properties of addition/subtraction and scalar multiplication of vectors to isolate $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6a-2x & =b \\\\ -2x & =b-6a \\\\ x & =-\\frac{1}{2}(b-6a) \\\\ x & =-\\frac{1}{2}([\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ -6 \\\\ -12 \\\\ -10\\end{aligned}]-6[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 8\\end{aligned}]) \\\\ x & =-\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}-16 \\\\ 6 \\\\ -48 \\\\ -58\\end{aligned}] \\\\ x & =[\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 24 \\\\ 29\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, ${x}_{3}-{x}_{4}=24-29=-5.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14061066/state.json" "file_sha256" "b4c3b9da0d15be78d0b279405751f68553deb47cd07086a9c5fb811a41ef3ce8"} {"question" "q-34601" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14061066/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c0622d23c841c058455643390172629c7022e8cd808bcfc52a771274e51e11bc"} {"question" "q-34601" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14061066/state.json" "file_sha256" "b4c3b9da0d15be78d0b279405751f68553deb47cd07086a9c5fb811a41ef3ce8"} {"question" "q-34601" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-4"] ["math" "-5"] ["math" "-53"] ["math" "5"] ["math" "53"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14061066/state.json" "file_sha256" "b4c3b9da0d15be78d0b279405751f68553deb47cd07086a9c5fb811a41ef3ce8"} {"question" "q-34601" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-5"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14061066/state.json" "file_sha256" "b4c3b9da0d15be78d0b279405751f68553deb47cd07086a9c5fb811a41ef3ce8"} {"question" "q-74006" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the vectors\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{3}=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIf ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3}=b,$ then what is ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14061066/state.json" "file_sha256" "b4c3b9da0d15be78d0b279405751f68553deb47cd07086a9c5fb811a41ef3ce8"} {"question" "q-74006" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "If ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3}=b,$ then   we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{3}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ 0 \\\\ {x}_{1}\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{2} \\\\ -{x}_{2} \\\\ -{x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -{x}_{3} \\\\ -3{x}_{3}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2} \\\\ -{x}_{2}-{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{1}-{x}_{2}-3{x}_{3}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the corresponding components, we get the following system:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}=-2 \\\\ -{x}_{2}-{x}_{3}=5 \\\\ {x}_{1}-{x}_{2}-3{x}_{3}=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe will solve this system using Gaussian elimination. First, we write the augmented matrix for this system:\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -1 & -1 & 5 \\\\ 1 & -1 & -3 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nRow-reducing the augmented matrix, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -1 & -1 & 5 \\\\ 1 & -1 & -3 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-1){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -1 & -1 & 5 \\\\ 0 & -3 & -3 & 3\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :=(-1){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & -5 \\\\ 0 & -3 & -3 & 3\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+3{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -12\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}=-2 \\\\ {x}_{2}+{x}_{3}=-5 \\\\ 0=-12.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHowever, the final equation $0=-12$  gives a false statement. So the system has no solution." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14061066/state.json" "file_sha256" "b4c3b9da0d15be78d0b279405751f68553deb47cd07086a9c5fb811a41ef3ce8"} {"question" "q-74006" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14061066/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c0622d23c841c058455643390172629c7022e8cd808bcfc52a771274e51e11bc"} {"question" "q-74006" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14061066/state.json" "file_sha256" "b4c3b9da0d15be78d0b279405751f68553deb47cd07086a9c5fb811a41ef3ce8"} {"question" "q-74006" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-12"] ["math" "-7"] ["math" "14"] ["math" "7"] ["text" "No solution"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14061066/state.json" "file_sha256" "b4c3b9da0d15be78d0b279405751f68553deb47cd07086a9c5fb811a41ef3ce8"} {"question" "q-74006" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "No solution"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14061066/state.json" "file_sha256" "b4c3b9da0d15be78d0b279405751f68553deb47cd07086a9c5fb811a41ef3ce8"} {"question" "q-74035" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the vectors\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{3}=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIf ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3}=b,$ then what is ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14061066/state.json" "file_sha256" "b4c3b9da0d15be78d0b279405751f68553deb47cd07086a9c5fb811a41ef3ce8"} {"question" "q-74035" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "If ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3}=b$, then we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{3}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ 0 \\\\ 3{x}_{1}\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-{x}_{2} \\\\ 5{x}_{2} \\\\ 2{x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ {x}_{3} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-{x}_{2} \\\\ 5{x}_{2}+{x}_{3} \\\\ 3{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the corresponding components, we get the following system:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-{x}_{2}=-3 \\\\ 5{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}=4 \\\\ 3{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}=-4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe will solve this system using Gaussian elimination. First, we write the augmented matrix for this system:\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 0 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 3 & 2 & 0 & -4\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nRow-reducing the augmented matrix, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 0 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 3 & 2 & 0 & -4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-3){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 0 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 0 & 5\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-1){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 0 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :=\\frac{1}{5}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 0 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0.2 & 0.8 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :=-{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 0 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0.2 & 0.8 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-{x}_{2}=-3 \\\\ {x}_{2}+\\,0.2{x}_{3}=0.8 \\\\ {x}_{3}=-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the third equation, we get ${x}_{3}=-1.$ Substituting this value into the second equation, we get \n\n$$\n{x}_{2}+0.2(-1)=0.8\\,⟹\\,{x}_{2}=1.\n$$\n\n   \n\nFinally,  substituting ${x}_{2}=1$ into the first equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}-(1)=-3\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=-2.\n$$\n\nSo, the solution of the system is ${x}_{1}=-2$, ${x}_{2}=1$, and ${x}_{3}=-1,$ which means  \n\n$$\n-2{a}_{1}+{a}_{2}-{a}_{3}=b.\n$$\n\nConsequently, \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}=-2+1-1=-2.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14061066/state.json" "file_sha256" "b4c3b9da0d15be78d0b279405751f68553deb47cd07086a9c5fb811a41ef3ce8"} {"question" "q-74035" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14061066/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c0622d23c841c058455643390172629c7022e8cd808bcfc52a771274e51e11bc"} {"question" "q-74035" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14061066/state.json" "file_sha256" "b4c3b9da0d15be78d0b279405751f68553deb47cd07086a9c5fb811a41ef3ce8"} {"question" "q-74035" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-2"] ["math" "-4"] ["math" "2"] ["math" "4"] ["text" "No solution"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14061066/state.json" "file_sha256" "b4c3b9da0d15be78d0b279405751f68553deb47cd07086a9c5fb811a41ef3ce8"} {"question" "q-74035" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-2"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14061066/state.json" "file_sha256" "b4c3b9da0d15be78d0b279405751f68553deb47cd07086a9c5fb811a41ef3ce8"} {"question" "q-105160" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the value of ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}$ given that $3a-5x=b$ and\n\n$$\na=[\\begin{aligned}-6 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}],\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}-13 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}].\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14061066/state.json" "file_sha256" "b4c3b9da0d15be78d0b279405751f68553deb47cd07086a9c5fb811a41ef3ce8"} {"question" "q-105160" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Using the properties of addition/subtraction and scalar multiplication of vectors to isolate $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3a-5x & =b \\\\ -5x & =b-3a \\\\ x & =-\\frac{1}{5}(b-3a) \\\\ x & =-\\frac{1}{5}([\\begin{aligned}-13 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]-3[\\begin{aligned}-6 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]) \\\\ x & =-\\frac{1}{5}[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -10 \\\\ -15\\end{aligned}] \\\\ x & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=-1+2=1.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14061066/state.json" "file_sha256" "b4c3b9da0d15be78d0b279405751f68553deb47cd07086a9c5fb811a41ef3ce8"} {"question" "q-105160" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14061066/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c0622d23c841c058455643390172629c7022e8cd808bcfc52a771274e51e11bc"} {"question" "q-105160" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14061066/state.json" "file_sha256" "b4c3b9da0d15be78d0b279405751f68553deb47cd07086a9c5fb811a41ef3ce8"} {"question" "q-105160" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-2"] ["math" "0"] ["math" "1"] ["math" "2"] ["math" "3"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14061066/state.json" "file_sha256" "b4c3b9da0d15be78d0b279405751f68553deb47cd07086a9c5fb811a41ef3ce8"} {"question" "q-105160" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "1"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14061066/state.json" "file_sha256" "b4c3b9da0d15be78d0b279405751f68553deb47cd07086a9c5fb811a41ef3ce8"} {"question" "q-105167" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the vectors\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}-7 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}-9 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIf ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}=b,$ then what is ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14061066/state.json" "file_sha256" "b4c3b9da0d15be78d0b279405751f68553deb47cd07086a9c5fb811a41ef3ce8"} {"question" "q-105167" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "If ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}=b$, then we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}-7 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-9 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}3{x}_{1} \\\\ -3{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{1}\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-7{x}_{2} \\\\ 5{x}_{2} \\\\ -{x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-9 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}3{x}_{1}-7{x}_{2} \\\\ -3{x}_{1}+5{x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{1}-{x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-9 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nEquating the corresponding components, we get the following system:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}3{x}_{1}-7{x}_{2}=-9 \\\\ -3{x}_{1}+5{x}_{2}=3 \\\\ {x}_{1}-{x}_{2}=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAdding the first and the second equations we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2{x}_{2} & =-6 \\\\ {x}_{2} & =3,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich we substitute into the second equation to get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-3{x}_{1}+5{x}_{2}=3 \\\\ -3{x}_{1}+5(3) & =3 \\\\ -3{x}_{1} & =-12 \\\\ {x}_{1} & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we substitute ${x}_{1}=4$ and ${x}_{2}=3$ into the third equation and obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-{x}_{2}=1 \\\\ (4)-(3) & =1 \\\\ 1 & =1,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich gives a true statement. \n\nSo the solution of the system is ${x}_{1}=4$ and ${x}_{2}=3,$ which means\n\n$$\n4{a}_{1}+3{a}_{2}=b.\n$$\n\nConsequently, \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=4+3=7.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14061066/state.json" "file_sha256" "b4c3b9da0d15be78d0b279405751f68553deb47cd07086a9c5fb811a41ef3ce8"} {"question" "q-105167" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14061066/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c0622d23c841c058455643390172629c7022e8cd808bcfc52a771274e51e11bc"} {"question" "q-105167" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14061066/state.json" "file_sha256" "b4c3b9da0d15be78d0b279405751f68553deb47cd07086a9c5fb811a41ef3ce8"} {"question" "q-105167" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "3"] ["math" "4"] ["math" "5"] ["math" "6"] ["math" "7"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Dev